{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1524526-mekhet-and-daeva-as-bloodlines-vtm","id":1524526,"title":"Mekhet and Daeva as bloodlines VTM","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2023-10-26T08:47:41-07:00","id":1524526,"title":"Mekhet and Daeva as bloodlines VTM","content":"Anyone have a good write up on Mekhet and Daeva as bloodlines in VtM 20 or even V5? Thanks","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27656-seth0194","name":"Seth0194","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-26T10:28:49-07:00","id":1524527,"title":"","content":"That's a good question. At some point White Wolf / Onyx Path published a <a href=\"https://preview.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/86202/vampire-translation-guide\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire Translation Guide</a> for using clans/covenants from VTR in VTM and vise versa. They don't give full stats, but they do give some suggestions. <br /> <br /> For the Daeva, they suggest giving them Potence, Presence and Celerity, keeping their weakness. And for the Mekhet Auspex, Celerity and Obfuscate, also keeping the weakness as is. So, basically not much conversion is needed.<br /> <br /> The Mekhet are my personal favorite clan. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7279-ichneumon","name":"Ichneumon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7279_6.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"14"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-26T23:36:50-07:00","id":1524571,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Seth0194</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1524526-mekhet-and-daeva-as-bloodlines-vtm#post1524526\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Anyone have a good write up on Mekhet and Daeva as bloodlines in VtM 20 or even V5? Thanks</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, none in particular afaik, but just disciplines and weakness are no big deal - and adapting some of the lore shouldn't be too hard.<br /> <br /> Daeva have the Brujah discipline set, with a weakness that is much closer to that of V20 Ravnos. Lore-wise, depending on what origin myth one proscribe to, one could either associate them with the Road of Sin (through many varied tales where they are portrayed as celebrants, seducers &amp; hedonists that die but rise to keep on going with the feast, bloodier than ever), Bahari (through Innana &amp; Lilith).<br /> <br /> <br /> Mekhet have same weakness as Setites, or a variant of the Haunted flaw, if one is messing with Hollow Mekhet instead. Either way it should be quite simple to exploit either or both weaknesses together their having Auspex to adapt/port over most of their Requiem lore under the excuse of being the legacy of Lazarus' blood or his own funeral ritual experiments.<br /> <br /> At least if one is playing with 1e Requiem stuff, that still is the one i'm most used to.<br /> The 2e Mekhet weakness, together Auspex &amp; Obfuscate, brings them an awfully close lot to VtM's Malks, i dare say.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1147,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","user":"Baaldam","date":". 10-27-2023, 09:10 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-28T06:07:42-07:00","id":1524634,"title":"","content":"I've considered how lore sheets could import some VtR clan features into V5, but it's tricky because some of them are clan weaknesses and some of them are enhancements of disciplines. I'm also inclined make certain disciplines combinations available.<br /> <br /> <b>Daeva</b><ul><li>You get to make your own Compulsion using a vice.</li> <li>Something about interacting with your herd or maybe gaining a Resonance bonus from building relationships with them.</li> <li>While using Presence, minor social penalties are cancelled out.</li> <li>You represent a zeitgeist, which effectively translates to fame, even if your personal identity is obscure.</li> <li>Gain Celerity or Potence as an in-clan discipline (the sheet would be for those that already have Presence).</li> </ul><b>Mekhet</b><ul><li>No reflection, fingerprints, recordings, etc. Unlike the old Lasombra weakness, it mystically goes unnoticed by those who have no reason to suspect it and unlike the V5 Lasombra weakness, it doesn't stop you from using electronics per se. It would be a shame to ignore that antagonistic reflection, but that might need some balancing.</li> <li>Obfuscate effects last until you say otherwise or do something that would normally end them, so you can even sleep hidden.</li> <li>Something about the open ended one and two dot Auspex powers.</li> <li>A bonus to the Premonition power when a personally preferred divination tool is used, like tarot cards or haruspicy.</li> <li>Something to do with Shadow Cults, although might be *basically* covered by the Osiris Predator Type.</li> <li>Gain Auspex, Celerity or Obfuscate as an in-clan discipline (the Auspex is for the benefit of Nosferatu, who fill some of Mekhet's niche. Maybe Banu Haqim too.)</li> </ul>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3523-spencer-from-the-hills","name":"Spencer from The Hills","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"546"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}